# Sprout backend — manual smoke requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP).
# Run register, copy the login token into @token, then call the protected route.

@base = http://localhost:4000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Register a merchant (defaults to onboarding / pending — never active)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "business_name": "Demo Store",
  "owner_name": "Ada Demo",
  "phone": "08031234567",
  "email": "ada@sprout.test",
  "password": "sprout-demo-1234"
}

### Login (returns { token, merchant })
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@sprout.test",
  "password": "sprout-demo-1234"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Protected route — with valid token
GET {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Protected route — no token (expect 401)
GET {{base}}/api/me
